# Independent Plan toolbar press states

Eliminate the remaining shared enlargement/highlight animation between Graph and Help.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Pressing Graph enlarges or highlights only Graph, never Help.
- [x] Pressing Help enlarges or highlights only Help, never Graph.
- [x] Releasing either control invokes only its own action.
- [x] Controls have separate visual/button identities outside any navigation container that couples their pressed animation.
- [x] Graph retains its current SCR-003 navigation availability and Help retains its contextual alert.
- [x] Both controls retain accessible labels and adequate independent hit regions.
- [x] Interaction regression coverage compiles for taps in both directions.
- [ ] Focused pressed-state checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- This supersedes TASK-018, whose separate `ToolbarItem` declarations did not fully isolate UIKit/SwiftUI enlargement feedback.

## Evidence

- Moved Graph and Help from navigation toolbar items into independent 44-point header buttons.
- Each control owns its own pressed background, scale animation, hit region, accessibility identity, and action.
- UI regression coverage asserts non-overlapping frames and taps Graph, Help, then Graph to detect cross-activation.
- `xcodebuild build-for-testing` compiled the app and both test bundles using `/private/tmp/Catanalyst-tasks025-030-derived`; live pressed-state verification remains manual.
